12.0pt;
  line-height:107%;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:A=
rial'>Algorithms
  matter because real-life tasks only become reusable, teachable, and
  programmable when they are broken into clear steps. A human can often inf=
er
  missing steps, but a computer cannot. If the directions are vague,
  incomplete, or out of order, the result becomes unreliable.</span></p>
