amily:
  Arial;color:#161616'>This lesson takes the step-count idea from Lesson 5 =
and
  zooms out. Instead of asking, 'How many steps does this exact tiny example
  take?' complexity asks, 'What happens when the problem gets bigger?' That=
 is
  the question that matters in real programs, because your code may handle 5
  contacts, 500 photos, or 50,000 records depending on the situation.</span=
></p>
