12.0pt;
  line-height:107%;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:A=
rial;
  color:#212121'>For this week, do not memorize Big O like random alphabet
  soup. Treat it like a growth story: when the input gets bigger, does the =
work
  stay flat, grow one step at a time, grow in pairs, or explode into repeat=
ed
  doubling? That growth pattern is what tells you whether an algorithm will
  still feel reasonable when the data gets large.</span></p>
