pt;
  line-height:107%;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:A=
rial;
  color:#212121'>When two solutions have different Big O, the better-scaling
  option often matters more as input grows. When two solutions have the same
  Big O, readability becomes a major deciding factor. Safe algorithms also
  check bad or unusual inputs before those inputs crash the code.</span></p>
